Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 20:22:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 082/154] feat(settings): the Appearance pane picks the app
 icon and the Dock follows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Swift package took the picker and its Dock consumer with it. Only the
appIconVariant setting survived, so a user could not pick an icon and a
hand-edited value changed nothing.

The pane shows the 21 tiles, served through the chrome://atrium request
filter from Contents/Resources/atrium-icons, which inject-icns.sh stages.
A click writes appIconVariant. At startup and after a save the browser
reads the PNG on the thread pool and sets applicationIconImage. A reply
for an older pick cannot overwrite a newer one. A stored slug that the
list retired still lets a click pick a new one.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

